<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Liberians United for Reconciliation and Democracy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1999">1999</a>–<a href="/years/2003">2003</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as LURD</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Liberians United for Reconciliation and Democracy (LURD) was a rebel movement that fought the government of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-taylor-liberia">Charles Taylor</a> from 1999, beginning the Second Liberian Civil War. Backed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guinea">Guinea</a>, it advanced on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/monrovia">Monrovia</a> in 2003, and with the MODEL rebels forced Taylor to resign and go into exile. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/accra">Accra</a> peace agreement of 2003 ended the war.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/liberians-united-for-reconciliation-and-democracy.jpg" alt="Liberians United for Reconciliation and Democracy" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: United States Army Africa · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:LURD_Gen_Cobra_with_security_at_port.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
